From 09af22d8fe44df3864dc4565fb4bf93db0878686 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:25:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(pagination): jump-to-page never accepted a number

Pagination.jsx tested the jump value with /^\\d+$/ (a literal backslash + 'd') and set pattern="\\d+" on the input, so no page number validated: Go did nothing / the browser blocked the form. Use /^\d+$/ and pattern="[0-9]*", and show an inline alert for non-numbers and out-of-range pages.
